Third-party notices
-------------------
glyphsift has no runtime dependency to install, but third-party Rust crates are compiled into the
artifacts it ships. This list was derived from `cargo tree -e normal --target all` for glyphsift-py (the wheel),
glyphsift-wasm (the npm package) and glyphsift-cli, with each licence read from `cargo metadata`
(Cargo.lock pins the exact versions). Each crate is used under the licence shown; where it offers a
choice (OR), glyphsift takes the permissive option named first in this file's table. The full licence text
of each crate is in its own source package on crates.io; the three crates that are not offered under Apache-2.0
(zmij, memchr and strsim (CLI only)) have their MIT text and copyright or author line reproduced at the end of this file.

Unicode data. Segmentation follows Unicode Standard Annex #29 (Unicode Text Segmentation), Copyright
Unicode, Inc., Unicode License v3 (Unicode-3.0). Compiled tables derived from the Unicode Character
Database ARE redistributed inside the wheel, the WASM and the CLI binary: unicode-segmentation carries the
grapheme-break tables and unicode-general-category 1.1.0 (Apache-2.0) carries the General_Category
tables (Unicode 16.0). No Unicode data files are shipped as files; only these compiled tables are.

